   "text": "This SMILES was written from my reading of the drawing, so it is not machine-checked. The gallium centre, the peptide stereochemistry and the odd ketone in the linker are the parts to check.\n\n**Ga-68 NODAGA chelate.** A 1,4,7-triazacyclononane ring carries three arms: two N-CH2-COO and one N-CH(COO)-CH2CH2-C(=O)-. Each carboxylate oxygen is bonded to Ga. Each ring nitrogen is shown as a dative bond to Ga, which I encoded as [N+] with [68Ga-3] so the formal charges balance and the whole species is neutral.\n\n**Central linker.** The chain runs CH(COO)\u2013CH2CH2\u2013C(=O)\u2013CH2\u2013CH, as drawn, including the ketone. The CH carries a C(=O)NH arm and a CH2CH2C(=O)NH arm. The wedge on this centre fixes it as [C@@H] in the SMILES order used.\n\n**Cyclic peptides.** Each is cyclo(Arg-Gly-Asp-D-Tyr-Lys), joined to the linker through the Lys side-chain NH. The ring order follows the drawing: Lys C=O to Arg NH, Arg C=O to Gly NH, Gly C=O to Asp NH, Asp C=O to Tyr NH, Tyr C=O to Lys NH. I assigned L-Arg, L-Asp, L-Lys and D-Tyr from the \"RGDyK\" name and the drawn wedges, then converted these to @/@@ by neighbour-order permutation. The left and right peptides are written identically.\n\n**Linker carbon with plain bonds.** The CH bearing the carboxylate on the NODAGA arm is drawn with plain bonds, so it has no stereo label.\n\nSMILES: [68Ga-3]%10%11%12%13%14OC(=O)C[N+]%101CC[N+]%11(CC(=O)O%13)CC[N+]%12(CC1)C(C(=O)O%14)CCC(=O)C[C@@H](C(=O)NCCCC[C@@H]2NC(=O)[C@@H](Cc3ccc(O)cc3)NC(=O)[C@H](CC(=O)O)NC(=O)CNC(=O)[C@H](CCCNC(=N)N)NC2=O)CCC(=O)NCCCC[C@@H]2NC(=O)[C@@H](Cc3ccc(O)cc3)NC(=O)[C@H](CC(=O)O)NC(=O)CNC(=O)[C@H](CCCNC(=N)N)NC2=O"
